      "body": "Size the speculative verify state-index table for both eager and CUDA graph batch padding. Graph alignment can exceed the eager maximum, leaving the existing table too short for padded verify batches.\n\nPreserve the row mapping for real requests and map additional padded positions to the existing reserved scratch row. This changes only the index-table length, not the state-buffer allocation or dtype.\n\nAdd CPU regression cases for graph-only padding, eager padding, and unpadded batches. Python syntax and diff checks passed; unit tests and GPU validation have not been run.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40526254004](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40526254004)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40526253693](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40526253693)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40526253546](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40526253546)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
